---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, ISSUES_URL } from '../consts';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of service: WP MCP"
  description="The terms governing use of wpmcp-pro.com and the WP MCP WordPress plugin: GPL licensing, the scope of the safety engine, warranties, and liability."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="sec-label">Legal</p>
      <h1>Terms of service.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        These terms govern your use of wpmcp-pro.com and the WP MCP
        WordPress plugin (published in source as <code>wpmcp</code>). WP MCP
        is a product of Fahad Murtaza / iSuperCoder ("we", "us"). By using
        this website, installing the plugin, or purchasing a Pro license,
        you agree to these terms. Questions are always welcome at
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="hero-fine mono">Last updated 26 July 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="legal">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>The software</h2>
      <p>
        WP MCP is distributed as source code on GitHub under the GNU General
        Public License v2 or later (GPL-2.0-or-later), the same license as
        WordPress itself. The core of the plugin, including the safety
        engine (snapshot, apply, verify, rollback) and the broad free tool
        surface, ships free. A Pro tier, billed through Freemius, adds
        premium features such as unlimited history and Elementor deep
        editing without changing the license of the underlying code.
      </p>

      <h2>Software license (GPL)</h2>
      <p>
        The GPL gives you the freedom to run, study, modify, and
        redistribute the plugin's code, including forking it. It does not
        extend to our trademarks: the WP MCP name and logo identify this
        specific project and are not covered by the GPL grant. A Pro license
        key controls access to premium feature activation, automatic
        updates, and support, separate from the GPL-licensed code itself;
        sharing, reselling, or circumventing the key system is not
        permitted.
      </p>

      <h2>Use of the plugin on your site</h2>
      <p>
        WP MCP runs entirely on your own WordPress installation and
        connects to an AI client of your choosing over the Model Context
        Protocol, authenticated by a WordPress application password you
        control. You are responsible for:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Which AI client you connect, and what permissions that connection carries.</li>
        <li>Backups of your own site, independent of WP MCP's snapshot/rollback engine, which is a change-recovery tool, not a full site backup solution.</li>
        <li>Complying with the terms of any AI provider (for example Anthropic or a Cursor-compatible client) you connect to your site.</li>
        <li>Reviewing which tools are enabled and which capabilities they require before granting write access on a production site.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What the safety engine does and does not guarantee</h2>
      <p>
        WP MCP's snapshot-and-restore engine covers a specific, documented
        set of object types: posts and pages (including WooCommerce products
        and menu items, which are posts under the hood), options, users,
        comments, and WooCommerce orders. A small set of deliberately risky
        operations, raw database row writes, guarded code execution, and
        permanent plugin/theme/file deletion, are disabled by default and,
        where enabled, honestly report when they are not recoverable rather
        than claiming an undo path that does not exist. Free-tier operation
        history is capped at the most recent 20 operations; a long AI agent
        session on the free tier can outrun that cap before it finishes. See
        the <a href="/docs.html">documentation</a> for the current, precise
        scope; we would rather you read exactly what is and is not covered
        than assume it covers everything.
      </p>

      <h2>Support</h2>
      <p>
        Support for the free plugin is provided on a best-effort basis
        through <a href={ISSUES_URL} rel="noopener">GitHub Issues</a>. Paid
        support terms for the Pro tier are described at checkout.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        You agree not to use the website or the plugin to break the law,
        infringe others' rights, distribute malware, or attempt to disrupt
        or gain unauthorized access to our services or those of others. You
        may not misrepresent a modified copy of the plugin as an official WP
